  'n35-vs-n52-neodymium-magnet-haptic-feel-guide': [
    {
      question: 'What do the neodymium magnet grades N35, N40, N45, N50, N52, and N54 mean?',
      answer: 'The "N" rating indicates the Maximum Energy Product (BHmax in Mega-Gauss-Oersteds, MGOe) of sintered NdFeB rare-earth magnets. An N52 magnet delivers ~48% higher magnetic pull force per cubic millimeter than an N35 magnet of identical dimensions.'
