      answer: 'Because unlimited sliders (such as FS-056, FS-075, FS-125, and FS-128) have no mechanical guide rails holding the two halves together, they rely entirely on high-flux N50–N54 magnet arrays (20 to 26 magnets) to prevent the top plate from flying off during rapid one-handed tricks.'
